## Summary

Afternoon supplement — three antibody/protein-design items today, all covered in full text. First, Tennenhouse/Fleishman (Weizmann, bioRxiv v2 posted 2026-07-13): **CADAbRe** — an end-to-end computational design pipeline for synthetic antibody repertoires. Combines all human V+J germlines with 141 experimental H3 loops, filters via CUMAb + independent A-Body-Builder-2 fold check (misfolding-prone flag when the two disagree), EpiNNet ML strategy selects freely-combinable germline+H3 sets. Golden Gate assembly gives 5×10⁸ designed Fabs at <$10⁻⁴ per variant. Panning against HEWL, SARS-CoV-2 RBD, mouse FLT3, and Lujo virus: 12 of 13 phage hits exactly match a designed sequence, EC50s 0.3–11 nM comparable to clinical benchmarks, developability suite (nanoDSF/BVP/AC-SINS/HIC) on par with 12 clinical-stage benchmark antibodies. Second, An/Cho/Kim (Yonsei + Institut Pasteur Korea, bioRxiv posted 2026-07-13): **mini-19** — de novo CD81-LEL binder via RFdiffusion + ProteinMPNN + AlphaFold2, with the specific methodological finding that truncated soluble receptor templates expose hydrophobic surfaces that fool single-ipTM filtering; multi-model backbone-convergence (≥2 of 5 AF2 models agree, ipTM>0.83) is what discriminates real hits. KD 0.5 nM, HCVcc IC50 1.2 nM, thermostable to 95°C, sibling mini-20 same scaffold 48× weaker. Third, Cao lab (Adv Sci published 2026-07-13; preprint bioRxiv 2026.03.20.713312): **HB148-M4** — four consensus SHMs (G26E/T28I/S53P/Y58F) mined by enrichment analysis of CoV-AbDab IGHV3-53 sequences with BA.1 neutralization data. Graft into germline HB148 restores ~100× KD to BA.1 RBD, neutralizes BA.1/BA.4-5 but not XBB.1.5; transferable to 3 of 4 other IGHV3-53 antibodies. Approximately additive per-position contributions imply distinct paratope-epitope contacts. Retrospective consensus-mining rather than de novo prediction, but a much more focused breadth-engineering strategy than DMS.

